[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2465822261","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98952#issuecomment-2465822261","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98952","id":2465822261,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6S-XY1","user":{"login":"girdenis-p","id":121173051,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzj0Ow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121173051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p","html_url":"https://github.com/girdenis-p","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-08T22:05:32Z","updated_at":"2024-11-08T22:06:24Z","body":"I see that the other platforms have loggers specific to the platform while the web OS just uses StdLogger. Emscripten offers access to the JS console through the console header <emscripten/console.h>. I managed to get a quick solution of this working using a custom logger and the console header from Emscripten:\r\n![Screenshot from 2024-11-08 21-58-53](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0cb2c5af-bdb6-4323-8d9e-3f45db3557ba)\r\nWould this be an appropriate solution? If so, I could working on writing up a PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2465822261/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468617369","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98952#issuecomment-2468617369","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98952","id":2468617369,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TJByZ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T16:48:53Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T16:49:58Z","body":"> Would this be an appropriate solution? If so, I could working on writing up a PR.\r\n\r\nSounds good to me :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\nMy WIP implementation was way more hacky than that: https://github.com/Calinou/godot/commit/web-print-warnings-as-console-warn\r\nIt also didn't apply warning styling to the `at:` line below, although this could have been done by always marking the line after a warning as being a warning as well.\r\n\r\nIdeally, the `at:` line would be merged with the warning message above it (same for errors), so that it appears as a single warning/error in the filter.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468617369/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476583666","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98952#issuecomment-2476583666","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98952","id":2476583666,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tnary","user":{"login":"girdenis-p","id":121173051,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzj0Ow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121173051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p","html_url":"https://github.com/girdenis-p","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/girdenis-p/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T14:56:16Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T15:53:19Z","body":"This is the type of solution I meant originally: https://github.com/girdenis-p/godot/commit/4c5470ae1bd429237071fbaf130cb898c1fbd771\r\n\r\nBut I noticed that this would violate backwards compatibility since it would stop printing to stdout and stderr and it seems as though we need to print to stdout or stderr otherwise we could break onPrint and onPrintError in the [EngineConfig API](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/platform/web/html5_shell_classref.html#onPrint).\r\n\r\nIf my current implementation makes sense, I could use the base of it and instead of using the console.h functions, I could add some js wrapper functions that will preserve the behaviour of the onPrint and onPrintError functions.\r\n\r\nEDIT: Feel free to a start conversation on the commit if a part of the implementation doesn't make sense.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476583666/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476938865","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98952#issuecomment-2476938865","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98952","id":2476938865,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ToxZx","user":{"login":"Faless","id":1687918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODc5MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T16:52:50Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T16:52:50Z","body":"I'm not too keen on making all sort of \"cosmetic\" changes which obviously results in bigger binaries/JS, but indeed the proper solution if we want to do this (and accept the ever growing size) is to implement a custom logger like the other platforms, and expose our own log functions as part of `library_godot_os.js`.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476938865/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]